\title{duckdt: Query DuckDB Using data.table Syntax}
\description{
Provides a data.table-style '[i, j, by]' interface backed by DuckDB. Expressions are translated to SQL and executed inside DuckDB, so data never needs to be pulled into R until the result is materialized as a data.table. Also reverse-engineers a database into a data model -- tables, columns, keys and references -- and draws it as an interactive entity-relationship diagram that builds the query for the tables and columns you pick.
